@title Parts pass: after a macro, the toast opens the Devices drawer on devices without a part (1920)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1920x1080
# Workflow gap row 5: placing a macro leaves devices without parts; one toast takes you to them.
click_text "New project"
wait 20
key ctrl+k
# The command, not a macro's name (a name picks that macro already).
text "place macro"
wait 5
key Enter
wait 10
# The Place macro window docks at the right edge: its search field is at x 1759 at this width.
click 1759 103
wait 4
text motor starter dol
wait 5
click_text "Motor starter DOL" Label
wait 10
click_text Place Button
wait 20
expect "without a part"
shot offer-toast
click_text "Choose parts" Button
wait 15
# "Accept all (n)" exists only in the parts pass (the rail's button is "Accept all proposals").
expect "Accept all ("
expect "-K1"
shot pass-open
key Down
wait 3
key Enter
wait 5
shot pass-after-enter
